      "content": "Basic Structure of the Progress Bar"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "First, let's look at the basic structure and styling of the progress bar without any animations."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "html",
      "content": "1<body>\n2\n3    <div class=\"text\">Progress Bar</div>\n4    <div class=\"progress-container\">\n5        <div class=\"progress-bar\"></div>\n6    </div>\n7\n8</body>"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "css",
      "content": "1body {\n2    display: flex;\n3    flex-direction: column;\n4    justify-content: center;\n5    align-items: center;\n6    height: 100vh;\n7    gap: 20px;\n8    background-color: #f0f0f0;\n9}\n10\n11.progress-container {\n12    width: 300px;\n13    height: 30px;\n14    background-color: #ddd;\n15    border-radius: 15px;\n16}\n17\n18.progress-bar {\n19    height: 100%;\n20    border-radius: 15px;\n21    width: 0%; /* Will later be animated to simulate progress */\n22}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Browser Output"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "Static Progress Bar",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The above code creates a progress bar layout."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here, the <body> element is styled to center the content vertically and horizontally on the page, with a background color for contrast."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The progress-container is a fixed-size box with rounded corners and a light gray background #ddd. Inside this container, the progress-bar represents the actual progress, initially set to have a width of 0%."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Next, you'll add the keyframe animation to show the actual progress."
    },
